RF.put("questb:b43",{"8603":{"id":8603,"t":"Vestments of the Oracle","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the the Husk of the Old God, 2 Idols of Death, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Honored reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nHusk of the Old God C'Thun in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Death Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The unmentionable Old God slowly awakens from his slumber beneath Ahn'Qiraj. The terrible fate that awaits Azeroth could come in days or years; time has no meaning for beings of his power.\nWhen the stars are favorable, he will lash out against all living beings with terrible wrath. You must find him before then and find a way to bring his existence to an end.\nDo this and bring me a piece of his husk. I shall grant you armor no mortal has ever worn... armor fit for one who has slain a god!","rew":"You will receive:\nVestments of the Oracle\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"At his dwelling in Ahn'Qiraj, dread C'Thun awaits in slumber.","done":"I did not expect you to return from your attempt, ‹name›.\nYou've fulfilled a destiny greater than that of most immortal beings.\nBy slaying C'Thun you've not only saved all of Azeroth, you've also tipped the scales of cosmic events beyond your comprehension.\nAccept these vestments as a symbol of the glory and burden that will come as a consequence of your actions.\nMay their power aid you in the challenges that await you, god-slayer!\nStart Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Priest Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8603\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Vestments of the Oracle this quest\nBring the the Husk of the Old God, 2 Idols of Death, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nVethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8523":{"id":8523,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Runecloth Bandages!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 runecloth bandages to Keeper Moonshade at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n20 Runecloth Bandage","desc":"So it is that we come to discuss pressing matters yet again ‹class›. Once more I thank you for your previous efforts; it is not everyone who would give so selflessly. But there is still more work to do.\n‹name›, will you once more collect runecloth bandages and return them to me here?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"So it is that we come to discuss pressing matters yet again, ‹class›. Once more I thank you for your previous efforts; it is not everyone who would give so selflessly. But there is still more work to do.\n‹name›, will you once more collect runecloth bandages and return them to me here?","done":"This is a fine road we are traveling together, ‹name›. You make an excellent working companion. Once more do I give thanks to you for your efforts on behalf of the entire Alliance. Come and talk again with me soon.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.8,"y":33.6,"n":"Keeper Moonshade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"523":{"id":523,"t":"Baron's Demise","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Head of Baron Vardus to Magistrate Maleb in Southshore.\nHead of Baron Vardus Baron Vardus","desc":"The contract you recovered was signed by Baron Vardus, a noble of the former kingdom of Alterac, and one known for a cold heart and brutal practices. I'm not surprised someone like the Baron was behind this.\nFind this man. Find him, and bring him to justice. He must be among the Syndicate haunts - perhaps at the ruins of Strahnbrad, or perhaps within the valley north of them.","rew":"Money: 1 1 gold, 0 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Baron Vardus cannot think Southshore will allow him to send his thugs against us with impunity. I want his head!","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. My head rests a little easier, knowing that villain lost his.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":48.1,"y":59.1,"n":"Magistrate Henry Maleb","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"7163":{"id":7163,"t":"Rise and Be Recognized","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Frostwolf Insignia Rank 1","desc":"<Warmaster Laggrond salutes you.>\nIt is your time, ‹name›. You have done much for the Frostwolf Clan and in doing so, earned a place as not only a soldier of Frostwolf but also as a friend.\nWell done! Present your initiate's insignia.","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostwolf Insignia Rank 2\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"<Warmaster Laggrond salutes you.>\nIt is your time, ‹name›. You have done much for the Frostwolf Clan and in doing so, earned a place as not only a soldier of Frostwolf but also as a friend.\nWell done! Present your initiate's insignia.","done":"This new insignia reflects your rank amongst the Frostwolf. Keep it on you at all times.\nAnd ‹class›... Die with honor!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":62.3,"y":58.9,"n":"Warmaster Laggrond","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8123":{"id":8123,"t":"Cut Arathor Supply Lines","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,650 experience instead of 8,150, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Deathstalker Mortis at Hammerfall.\nArathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"The League of Arathor is sparing no expense in their move to retake Arathi. They, and all the races of the Alliance, now stream to this distant region, intent on expanding their hold from Refuge Pointe. We must stop them, and the best means to stop them is to take their supplies.\nYou can help us, ‹name›. Enter Arathi Basin, known for its rich mines, fertile land and skilled craftsman. Capture and control every base you can, win the battle, and return to me with the resources you gain.","rew":"Money: 2 50 2 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650\n+200 reputation with The Defilers\nLevel 55 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 51 53 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 8123","cats":["arathi-basin"]},"8443":{"id":8443,"t":"Conquering Arathi Basin","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Our conflict with the Alliance has escalated to a true war. No longer are false pretenses to enter into battle used or expected by either side at this point.\nThe battle for the Arathi Basin is one of resources, plain and simple. Either the Alliance gets the resources and uses them against us or we get them and use them to keep our war efforts going. Help the Defilers maintain the flow of resources we need, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+50 reputation with The Defilers","back":"You've come back with news from Arathi, ‹class›?","done":"Securing our resources in Arathi is an important task! You've done well, ‹name›.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"3563":{"id":3563,"t":"Jes'rimon's Payment to Jediga","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Jes'rimon's Note to Jediga in Azshara.\nJes'rimon's Note\nProvided: Jes'rimon's Note","desc":"Take this letter to Jediga. Let her know that our deal has been beneficial and I be pleased with her work.\nYou tell her she come back to Orgrimmar fast and Jes'rimon make sure he take good care of her.\nTell her that, and maybe in the future I have need of your services again, ‹name›.","rew":"Money: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,800","back":"Have you spoken to Jes'rimon yet?\nHe's a boar among trolls, but his information is usually accurate and his jobs well paying.\nIf you can stand his attitude then you stand to make some good coin from his business endeavors.","done":"I can see he was more than pleased by the looks of his note.... a little too pleased.\nPerhaps some day I'll take time to make sure he knows how much I appreciate his advances also. Well, at least there's one reason to look forward to spending more time in Azshara.\nHere's your share of our payment.\nOrgrimmar Azshara","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":55.5,"y":34.1,"n":"Jes'rimon","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":22.6,"y":51.4,"n":"Jediga","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"2203":{"id":2203,"t":"Badlands Reagent Run II","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the empty thaumaturgy vessels on scorched guardian dragons found in the Badlands. Once you have them filled, bring them to Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath.\n3 Vessel of Dragon's Blood\nProvided: Thaumaturgy Vessel Lockbox","desc":"You have been most helpful to me, ‹class›. I would reward you with the very recipe for the brew I gave you earlier... but I would ask of you a task that is quite dangerous. Hear my request.\nThis lockbox contains three empty thaumaturgy vessels; they are imbued with an attunement aura that will drain the blood of a scorched guardian dragon. Using one on the beast will anger it greatly, so be warned. Once you have all three filled, bring them to me.\nDo this, and the recipe will be yours.","rew":"You will learn: Restorative Potion\nExperience: 3,750\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Have you used the vessels to get me the scorched guardian dragon blood I need? Yes, I know it is a dangerous task... but the recipe for my restorative brew awaits your success. Risk and reward, my friend... risk and reward...","done":"From one alchemist to another, I salute you. Here, take this recipe and commit it to your knowledge. May it bring you the success and rewards that it has brought me over the years.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":2.4,"y":46.1,"n":"Jarkal Mossmeld","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"4123":{"id":4123,"t":"The Heart of the Mountain","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Heart of the Mountain to Maxwort Uberglint in the Burning Steppes.\nThe Heart of the Mountain Heart of the Mountain","desc":"For years I have sought a certain gem. It is called the Heart of the Mountain and it's the size of your fist! The Dark Iron dwarves have it locked in their vault and, try as I may, they won't let me purchase it.\nSo I must resort to force.\nFight your way to the Lower Vault of Blackrock Depths, breach its secret safe and gain the Heart. To do that, you must defeat Watchman Doomgrip, and he won't appear until you've opened every relic coffer in the vault!\nGood luck.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650","back":"Do you have the Heart of the Mountain? To me, its value is without limit.","done":"You have the heart! Amazing! It is even more beautiful than I imagined!\nPlease, ‹name›, take this as payment!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65.2,"y":23.9,"n":"Maxwort Uberglint","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4363":{"id":4363,"t":"The Princess's Surprise","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Ironforge and speak with King Magni Bronzebeard.","desc":"Thaurissan was a great and honorable dwarf. You ruined my life and the life of my unborn child!\n<You think that Princess Bronzebeard may still be suffering from the residual effect of the Emperor's spell.>\nReturn to Ironforge and tell my father that the heir to the Kingdom of Ironforge will be a Dark Iron dwarf.\nWhether he approves or not, it shall be.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMagni's Will Songstone of Ironforge\nMoney: 2 65 2 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,650","done":"<King Magni Bronzebeard is visibly upset.>\nIt seems that even in death, Thaurissan has won.\nYou are dismissed, ‹name›. Before you leave, you may choose your reward from the royal vault.\n<King Bronzebeard slumps into his throne to mull over this bizarre change of events.>","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.4,"y":30.1,"n":"King Magni Bronzebeard","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"2763":{"id":2763,"t":"The Art of the Imbue","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring forty Mithril Bars and four Citrines to Galvan the Ancient in Stranglethorn.\n40 Mithril Bar\n4 Citrine Zalas Witherbark 7.1 % , Wandering Protector 3.1 % , Ruul Onestone 2 % , Darbel Montrose 1.4 % and 4 more","desc":"The harvesting of precious gems is of utmost importance to our craft, ‹name›. Few gems are more precious than the citrine. The magical properties we imbue into our goods are amplified greatly by the presence of citrine.\nFor this lesson, we will fortify forty bars of mithril with four citrines. The result will be a better understanding of magical gemology and the knowledge to create ornate mithril shoulders.","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Ornate Mithril Shoulders\nExperience: 3,900","back":"After such mining, your muscles bulge and your body aches!","done":"One can barely keep their eyes from leaving its splendor, ‹name›. Aye, citrine is a glorious gem.\nPay attention and learn what such a discovery may teach us!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":50.6,"y":20.5,"n":"Galvan the Ancient","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"2603":{"id":2603,"t":"Vulture's Vigor","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring ten Vulture Gizzards and two Snickerfang Jowls to Bloodmage Lynnore.\n10 Vulture Gizzard Black Slayer 40 % , Spiteflayer 30 %\n2 Snickerfang Jowl Starving Snickerfang 40 % , Snickerfang Hyena 40 % , Ravage 30 %","desc":"Death does indeed have wings in these blasted lands, ‹race›. I have witnessed the black slayers and bonepickers feasting upon the corpse of many a fallen explorer - sometimes feeding upon the most vile and disease ridden of carcasses. It is a wonder, then, how their internal systems overcome the pestilence that claims these lands.\nAssist me in my studies, ‹name›! Gizzards I need! Two snickerfang jowls will also be required for the base of the concoction.\nYou shall be rewarded two-fold for your efforts.","rew":"You will receive:\nGizzard Gum\nExperience: 4,700","back":"Do not waste my time, ‹name›. We have nothing to discuss, unless you have recovered the items I have requested.","done":"Most excellent! I shall get to work immediately. Perhaps a cure for many of the ailments of the world is to be found!\nAh yes, your reward - of course, should you require more of the gum, return to me and another task you shall be given.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":50.6,"y":14.3,"n":"Bloodmage Lynnore","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"4283":{"id":4283,"t":"FIFTY! YEP!","lv":56,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Oralius wants 50 Blackrock Medallions. Chances are high that these medallions can be found on the orcs in the Burning Steppes.\n50 Blackrock Medallion Blackrock Worg 45 % , Ember Worg 45 % , Slavering Ember Worg 45 % , Giant Ember Worg 45 % and 4 more","desc":"I'm going to let you in on a little secret, soldier. Come a little closer.\nI'M THE ONLY SANE ONE HERE!\nLook at these people! Would you believe that they're all insane!? Well they are! NUTS! CRAZY!\n<Oralius lowers his voice.>\nLet's just keep that between me, you, and my pal Captain Winky.\n<Oralius grabs at the air and squeezes.>\nAnyhooooo... I'm collecting badges to go along with my ogre ear collection. Orc is the flavor of the day. Fifty. GO!\n<Oralius blows into a horn.>\nSHIP IT!","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,800\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"<Oralius is talking into a rather large, severed ogre ear.>\nBurning Steppes to control, come in control.","done":"You've done it! Your reward is: RUB MY BELLY! GO ON! RUB IT!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.6,"y":68.7,"n":"Oralius","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97963":{"id":97963,"t":"Camping 101 alchemy","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Nyassa Swiftdraught in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your alchemy skill to 20","desc":"So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.","back":"Yes, I can teach you.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Mana Well. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.6,"y":43.4,"n":"Nyassa Swiftdraught","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94283":{"id":94283,"t":"Craftsmans writ goblin land mine","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Goblin Land Mine\nGoblin Land Mine","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Goblin Land Mine, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Goblin Land Mine Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94283","cats":["crafting"]},"7883":{"id":7883,"t":"The World's Largest Gnome!","lv":60,"min":20,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. No longer rewards Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket.","obj":"3 Barbaric Harness","back":"Yebb Nebblegear is looking to add more talent to his show, and he's searching far and wide for the world's largest gnome. Do you know any gnomes of considerable size?\nWell before he finds the gnome, he wants to have its costume ready. I think a barbaric harness would be a good foundation for the costume; can you make some harnesses and bring them to me? Do that, and I'll have a stack of Darkmoon Faire tickets for you...","done":"Oh dear, these are quite large!! I can't imagine finding a gnome that would fit snuggly into them, but not to worry - if the gnome we find is not big enough, I can make adjustments to his costume.\nMany thanks, ‹name›. Here are the tickets I promised you.\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.6,"y":70.8,"n":"Chronos","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":37.2,"y":42.5,"n":"Chronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"1003":{"id":1003,"t":"Buzzbox 525","lv":16,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 4 Grizzled Scalps from Grizzled Thistle Bears to the south of Auberdine and place them in Buzzbox 525.\n4 Grizzled Scalp Grizzled Thistle Bear 40 % , Den Mother 40 %","desc":"Over the boiling noises and dripping sounds coming from the machine, you hear Wizbang's wavering voice call out.\n\"Nexsht onesh far south down the road. Shouldn't be hard to find... jusht off to the shide... near a fensh. I think I hid it in shum bushesh... Bushessh. Hehehe... Yesh, Buzzbox 525 takes grizzled scalps from thoshe grizzled thistle bears. Boy thash a mouthful. Grizzshled... Hehehe...\"\nYou hear more gulping sounds as the machine cuts out. Then, suddenly, it bursts back to life.\n\"4!\"","rew":"You will receive:\nWizbang's Gunnysack 5 Wizbang's Special Brew\nMoney: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"You hear singing coming from Buzzbox 525.\n\"Though crawler wine's shweet, and thresher ale fine, and moonstalker moonshine ish grand. There's nothing sho dear, as a thistle bear beer, and shoon I shall have shome on hand!\"\nThe hatch is open and awaits the 4 grizzled scalps as you hear the song repeated over and over.","done":"\"Sho yash gotsh the scalps in? That'sh sho great... Wha? Well, yesh I shuppose ya have realized that I can speaksh to ya without the materials in the machine. But I was telling the truth when I shaid they were broken!\nSee, in addition to being communimacation toolsh, the Buzzboxes also brew and distill fine liquor. Shorry for any deceptshion, but the nightelves do not apprecimerate my liquor trade in their townsh. I put shomething special in thish box to show my gratitude for yer effortsh. Enjoy!\"","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":51.3,"y":24.6,"n":"Buzzbox 323","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":41.4,"y":80.6,"n":"Buzzbox 525","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"4763":{"id":4763,"t":"The Blackwood Corrupted","lv":18,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fill the Empty Cleansing Bowl at the Auberdine Moonwell.\nGather a sample of fruit, nut, and grain from the northern Blackwood furbolg camps.\nMix the bowl and place it near the bonfire closest to the Cliffspring River at the northern camp, thus summoning the satyr corruptor.\nTake the Talisman of Corruption and bring it to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine.\nTalisman of Corruption Xabraxxis' Demon Bag\nProvided: Empty Cleansing Bowl","desc":"We've learned that a source of furbolg corruption is from the satyr. They hold sway via talismans that they channel magic through. If the furbolg have a chance at salvation, we must lure out the satyr corruptor and take that talisman!\nFill this bowl at our moonwell and take samples of the furbolgs' food from their northern camp. Mix them and place it near the bonfire by the river; any furbolgs who eat will be cleansed just long enough to lure out the satyr corruptor... who then you must slay!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMoonstone Wand Wildkeeper Leggings Guststorm Legguards\nMoney: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,700\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The Talisman of Corruption is a sinister device that only serves to pervert the balance of nature. When you obtain this item from whatever satyr is tormenting the furbolgs and bring it to me for disposal, we will have won a great victory this day!","done":"We have just begun this war to reclaim our forest from the forces of corruption, but a battle this day has been won! ‹name›, the people of Auberdine owe you a debt of gratitude that will never be easily repaid. Please accept this along with our thanks. What we have learned here today may one day free our furbolg friends from the shackles of torment permanently.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":40.1,"n":"Thundris Windweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"3803":{"id":3803,"t":"Morrowgrain to Darnassus","lv":55,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 550 experience instead of 4,700, 0.12 times as much.","obj":"10 Morrowgrain","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Circle Cache\nExperience: 550\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The Arch Druid is always looking for additional morrowgrain for the Cenarion Circle's continued research. We take them in increments of ten, and award you with a cache of goods you should find useful. When you have ten, let me know and I will reward you accordingly.","done":"Excellent - this morrowgrain will no doubt please the Arch Druid. I must admit though... just being near them makes me feel a little uncomfortable. I can only imagine how difficult it is for the Arch Druid to tolerate them in such large numbers!\nThis is for you, ‹name›. The Cenarion Circle thanks you for your continued support.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"7483":{"id":7483,"t":"Libram of Rapidity","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 54 instead of 58.","obj":"Bring a Libram of Rapidity, 1 Pristine Black Diamond, 2 Large Brilliant Shards, and 2 Blood of Heroes to Lorekeeper Lydros in Dire Maul to receive an Arcanum of Rapidity.\nLibram of Rapidity Prince Tortheldrin 2 % , Magister Kalendris 2 % , Illyanna Ravenoak 2 % , Tendris Warpwood 2 % and 4 more\nPristine Black Diamond Veteran Commando 2.3 % , Witherbark Speaker 1 % in Zul'Gurub , Winterax Axe Thrower 1 % , Lady Illucia Barov 1 % in Scholomance and 4 more\n2 Large Brilliant Shard\n2 Blood of Heroes Blood of Heroes","desc":"Master Winthalus lost the Libram of Rapidity in the east wing. The Libram will allow for a minor haste cantrip to be placed upon your equipment. Parlor tricks, really...\nRegardless, if you are interested, you will need to present the Libram along with some basic reagents.\nHrm... I believe it also requires blood of heroes, a pristine black diamond, and large brilliant shards. I could be wrong!\n<Lydros shrugs.>","rew":"You will receive:\nArcanum of Rapidity\nExperience: 1,650\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"What is it? I have much cataloguing to do!","done":"<Lydros yawns.>\nAs promised, the Arcanum of Rapidity. Don't spend it all in once place.\n<Lydros snickers.>\nStart Lorekeeper Lydros End Lorekeeper Lydros Level 60 , requires level 54 Difficulty 54 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7483","cats":["dire-maul"]},"6123":{"id":6123,"t":"Gathering the Cure","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Earthroot and 12 Lunar Funguses to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine so she may make a curative salve.\n5 Earthroot Earthroot , Earthroot , Tattered Chest 6 % , Battered Chest 6 % and 4 more\n12 Lunar Fungus Lunar Fungal Bloom","desc":"The water will serve as the base of the curative salve I'll make for the deer. For curative properties, I need some earthroot. Herbalists know how to find it, so if we're unlucky and you aren't one then you'll need to find one to help us out.\nFinally for potency, I need some lunar fungus. Finding lunar fungal blooms is easy enough; they're all over the place in caves just to the east of here. Moonkin reside in the caves and they're irritable as of late, so be careful.","rew":"Experience: 750\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Have you got the reagents I need to make the salve? The deer aren't getting any better on their own, so we better hurry to help them out!","done":"This is good, ‹name›, so much so that it should be enough to make some ample doses of the salve - at least enough to start to make a difference.\nMaking a cure for poisons can be quite difficult at times because each one often requires a very specific antidote to counteract it. Imagine being able to cure a poison at will without having to worry about the exact ingredients of what the antidote must be!\nNow, let me get to work on this!","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.7,"y":40.7,"n":"Alanndarian Nightsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"1323":{"id":1323,"t":"The Black Shield","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk with Krog in Brackenwall Village.","desc":"Oh, I think I might have dropped too much acid onto the shield. Let me just rub a little...\nHm, kind of hard to read, but it looks like the name Mosarn. Never heard of him. Maybe Krog knows. Krog knows many people.","rew":"Experience: 1,400","done":"Mosarn? Sounds familiar... I can't put my finger on it. Maybe it'll come to me later.\nIt probably isn't important. A shield can come from anywhere and not mean anything...","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.5,"y":30.8,"n":"Do'gol","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.4,"y":31.9,"n":"Krog","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"91723":{"id":91723,"t":"Delicate instruments","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill 8 Kobold Geomancers in Jasperlode Mine, then return to Hamish Bergwort in the Tower of Azora.\nKobold Geomancer slain : 0/ 8","desc":"Blast it! Every time I try to calibrate these sensitive arcane instruments, they get thrown off again by a surge of energy.\nThe surges seem to be coming from the north, where those primitive Kobolds have been practicing their crude magic. Could you clear some of them out, so I can continue my work?","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Well done, my friend. Let me try my calibrations again...","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":65,"y":69.8,"n":"Hamish Bergwort","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"123":{"id":123,"t":"The Collector","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire and give him The Collector's Schedule.\nThe Collector's Schedule\nProvided: The Collector's Schedule","desc":"This note is a schedule with a list of days and times when a person -- described only as \"The Collector\" -- will receive a shipment of gold from the mines in Elwynn Forest.\nFrom the schedule, it looks as if the Collector resides near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn.\nThis sounds important. You should report it to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 0 silver, 85 copper Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What?!? We haven't had our people working the Elwynn mines for months!\nLet me see that note you have...","done":"Hm... I have heard of this \"Collector\" but I don't know whom he's working for. Thank you for the schedule. It will help us solve this mystery.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":65.9,"n":"Marshal Dughan","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3643":{"id":3643,"t":"Show Your Work","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Mithril Tubes, an Accurate Scope, and a 2 Advanced Target Dummies to Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay.\n6 Mithril Tube\nAccurate Scope\n2 Advanced Target Dummy","desc":"As your mentor, I want some samples of your work. You're a skilled engineer; there is no question of this, ‹name›. What I hope to do though is to analyze your work for ways to emphasize gnome-oriented techniques in your future efforts. I need the following samples: six mithril tubes, an accurate scope, and two advanced target dummies.\nSubmit these items to me and I will issue you your own Gnome Engineer Membership Card; it is required for access to all gnome engineering trainers!","rew":"You will receive:\nGnome Engineer Membership Card\nYou will learn: Gnomish Engineer\nExperience: 3,150\n+75 reputation with Engineering - Gnome","back":"Once I receive your crafted engineering items for my review, I will hand you a genuine Gnome Engineer Membership Card! So long as the card is valid, you will have unlimited access to any gnome engineer trainer anywhere in the world.","done":"Here is your first Gnome Engineer Membership Card!\nThis card has its dues paid for in advance for fourteen days; all cards expire after two weeks of activity. When it does, pay your next set of dues to any gnome engineer trainer in order to get another card; without the card, your membership will temporarily lapse and you cannot access new schemata.\nThis never affects what you already know; once a gnome engineer, always a gnome engineer.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.4,"y":76.4,"n":"Oglethorpe Obnoticus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"2523":{"id":2523,"t":"Corrupted Songflower","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply some Cenarion plant salve to the songflower. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":52.9,"y":87.8,"n":"Corrupted Songflower","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4443":{"id":4443,"t":"Corrupted Whipper Root","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a whipper root plant. The visible roots of the plant appear tough and leathery, and a slimy film hangs from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply 3 Cenarion Plant Salves to the Whipper Root. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":50.6,"y":18.3,"n":"Corrupted Whipper Root","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"5883":{"id":5883,"t":"Salve via Mining","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Tainted Vitriol Gold Vein 50 % , Ooze Covered Gold Vein 50 % , Gold Vein 50 % , Mithril Deposit 50 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"If you possess a Cenarion beacon while mining in Felwood, you will be able to see tainted vitriol that corrupts a vein of raw metal. I know how to purify that vitriol and turn it into a reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. You will then use that salve on plants you find in the wild that need saving.\nIf you have collected any tainted vitriol, I'll give you some Cenarion plant salve I have already prepared.","done":"Very well then, here's some Cenarion plant salve. If you find more vitriol when you mine in Felwood, remember to hold on to it for me! The more of it you find, the more salve I will be able to make.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":54.1,"y":86.8,"n":"Arathandris Silversky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"7003":{"id":7003,"t":"Zapped Giants","lv":48,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use Zorbin's Ultra-Shrinker to zap any kind of giant found in Feralas into a more manageable form. Bring 15 Miniaturization Residues found on the zapped versions of these giants to Zorbin Fandazzle at the docks of the Forgotten Coast, Feralas.\n15 Miniaturization Residue Zapped Cliff Giant , Zapped Wave Strider , Zapped Land Walker , Zapped Shore Strider and 1 more\nProvided: Zorbin's Ultra-Shrinker","desc":"I'm going to have to do something about the giants if I stay out here! They're certainly not good for business, now are they?\nI've been working on a variant of a gnomish shrinking ray, but I'm using superior GOBLIN technological advances in its construction! In an effort to avoid inconveniences for myself such as death, I'd like for you to try it out on any of the giants in Feralas. You should find miniaturization residue on them after you shrink them - bring me back some!","rew":"You will receive:\nZorbin's Mega-Slicer\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+150 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"Miniaturization residue, I assure you, is a valuable commodity when it comes to engineering! Well, it is valuable in that it helps me make sure the zapper won't do something as disappointing as explode on the user.\nOh, I mean for the zappers other than the one I gave you. Absolutely!","done":"Splendifimous! Not only am I glad to see that you've returned with the residue, but also with all your major appendages intact! That is, well, there was never any danger in using the Ultra-Shrinker, now was there!\nI do appreciate your effort on my behalf, ‹name›. Truly, you are a friend to goblins everywhere. Accept this as a token of my appreciation!","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":44.8,"y":43.4,"n":"Zorbin Fandazzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2923":{"id":2923,"t":"Tinkmaster Overspark","lv":26,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge.","desc":"Tinkmaster Overspark is very upset with the fate of his mechanical creation, Techbot. I remember Techbot as a kind and helpful tool for the gnomes, but Overspark tells me it's malfunctioned.\nVery sad. But with luck perhaps he can be fixed!\nSpeak with Tinkmaster Overspark, in Tinker Town in Ironforge. He would welcome your help.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"Yes it's true. Techbot has gone rogue! Please, can you help me?\nStormwind City Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.1,"y":48.4,"n":"Brother Sarno","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.2,"y":29.2,"n":"Tinkmaster Overspark","e":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"4603":{"id":4603,"t":"More Sparklematic Action","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -1g -3s instead of 0.","obj":"Grime-Encrusted Object Holdout Technician 25 % , Holdout Medic 25 % , Holdout Warrior 25 % , Irradiated Pillager 25 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nSparklematic-Wrapped Box","back":"The Sparklematic 5200 is empty, awaiting a grime-encrusted object to clean and three silver coins to start!","done":"The Sparklematic 5200 comes to life, lurching to and fro. Inside, the helpless grime that has encrusted the object placed within it is being pulverized by the machine's gnomish cleaning agent.\nThe Sparklematic 5200 comes to a halt, heralded by a familiar \"ding!\" The item receptacle of the machine spirals open, revealing a neatly wrapped box.\nStart The Sparklematic 5200 End The Sparklematic 5200 Level 30 , requires level 25 Difficulty 25 26 28 33 38 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 4603\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 30, 2,450 XP in all.\n1 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200!\nInsert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200!\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2,450 XP\n3 [ 30 ] More Sparklematic Action this quest\nThe Sparklematic 5200","cats":["gnomeregan"]},"2843":{"id":2843,"t":"Gnomer-gooooone!","lv":35,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Wait for Scooty to calibrate the Goblin Transponder.","desc":"As long as you have the transponder in your possession, all you need to do is step on the pad and you'll be teleported to Gnomeregan.\nYou may experience some unusual side effects, but none of those should be permanent... anymore.\nI almost forgot the most important part - getting back. When you're ready to come back, just step on the transpolyporter pad in Gnomeregan!\nNow to calibrate the transponder to your size and weight.","rew":"You will receive:\nGoblin Transponder","back":"It's ready!","done":"All done! When you're ready, just step on the pad.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.6,"y":77.5,"n":"Scooty","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"683":{"id":683,"t":"Sara Balloo's Plea","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Sara Balloo's note to King Magni Bronzebeard of Ironforge.\nSara Balloo's Plea\nProvided: Sara Balloo's Plea","desc":"‹name›, I have but a small request to ask of you.\nTake this note I have prepared to our great monarch of Ironforge, King Magni Bronzebeard. 'Tis a small task to ask of one such as yourself, someone who has shown great valor to the cause of the Alliance thus far.\nFor me to go before the King in my grief-ridden state would not serve the purpose of my cause. Surely you understand.","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"So you are ‹name› the ‹class›? News of your contributions to the Alliance has traveled quite far, you know?\nOn what business do you come before me today?","done":"It will take but a moment for me to peruse this letter...","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.3,"y":31.9,"n":"Sara Balloo","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.4,"y":30.1,"n":"King Magni Bronzebeard","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"3483":{"id":3483,"t":"Signal for Pickup","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nStandard Issue Flare Gun","done":"Ah, another flare gun, huh? That I can do.\nAnd don't forget, southern tip of Azshara. It's a small little island that's been turned into a landing pad. You can't miss it if you're in the right spot.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.5,"y":36.3,"n":"Xiggs Fuselighter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"7803":{"id":7803,"t":"A Donation of Silk","lv":60,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Silk Cloth Protector Weaver , Mountaineer Langarr 85.7 % , Watcher Wollpert 85.7 % , Mountaineer Zwarn 78.3 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"As with most other fabrics, our stocks of silk are at an all-time low. Our stores are such that we'd only need sixty pieces of silk from you total; we should be able to reach our goal with the support of others.\nA benevolent gift such as silk, might I add, would certainly increase your local standing in the community! If you have the sixty pieces of silk cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58,"y":26.2,"n":"Mistina Steelshield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"9003":{"id":9003,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Deliana your Devout Crown and Devout Robe.\nDevout Crown Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nDevout Robe General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"That's an amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved. Now maybe I'll be able to sleep at night with both eyes shut.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you'll really enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nVirtuous Crown Virtuous Robe\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Devout pieces in exchange for your new Virtuous Crown and Robe?","done":"I'm going to miss you, ‹name›. I owe you such a debt of gratitude; I think I'll never be able to repay it.\nI hope that you enjoy your new head and chest armor, and that it protects you for a long time to come.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"283":{"id":283,"t":"A Dark Threat Looms","lv":20,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"The Disarming Mixture seemed to take effect. Return to Chief Engineer Hinderweir to report the good news.","desc":"The keg fizzles slightly.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDwarven Tree Chopper Thornblade\nExperience: 1,950\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Thank you so much, ‹name›!! You have saved the Stonewrought Dam! Without your help, the Dark Iron terrorists would have surely seen to this mighty landmark's demise. You have made the Kingdom and the Alliance proud, brave ‹class›.\nThe Dam is once again safe. . . for the time being at least. . . .","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":50.6,"y":14.3,"n":"Explosive Charge","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":46,"y":13.6,"n":"Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8683":{"id":8683,"t":"Dawnstrider the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":64.5,"y":24,"n":"Elder Dawnstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1883":{"id":1883,"t":"Speak with Un'thuwa","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Un'thuwa.","desc":"Un'thuwa, tribal mage of Sen'jin Village, detects a disturbance in the magic currents of Durotar and asks for aid. Speak with Un'thuwa and do what you can to help him.\nDo this, and in time further secrets will be revealed to you.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Hail, ‹name›. Praise to you, for my call for aid is now answered. Let us hope you are up to the task...\nOrgrimmar Durotar","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":39.2,"y":86.3,"n":"Uthel'nay","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":56.3,"y":75.1,"n":"Un'Thuwa","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"9323":{"id":9323,"t":"Wild Fires in the Eastern Kingdoms","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 50.","obj":"Visit the Fire Festival camps located in Blasted Lands, Eastern Plaguelands, the Hinterlands and Searing Gorge, then speak with the Festival Flamekeeper.\nFlame of the Blasted Lands used\nFlame of the Plaguelands used\nFlame of the Hinterlands used\nFlame of Searing Gorge used","desc":"Our celebration of the flame is spread throughout the land, ‹class›. Not a single place remains untouched by the heat of this holiday, and the strongest fires burn a brilliant blue. Seek them out.\nYou'll find one just north of Blackrock Spire. The others are located deep within the Eastern Plaguelands near a decrepit town, along the road to the cliffs within the mountainous Hinterlands, and on the way to the Dark Portal within the Blasted Lands.\nReturn once your journey is done.","rew":"You will receive:\nMantle of the Fire Festival 10 Burning Blossom\nExperience: 3,300","back":"It will take time to prevail against this threat. How have you fared, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, here you are. A little wearier, a bit dustier, but enlightened! The heat touches us all during this season and unites us; your very being glows with the power of the fires you touched. Ah, but these days enlightenment is taken as a rather poor reward for being sent on a task, I suppose. Take these, then, and enjoy the celebration.\nOrgrimmar Tirisfal Glades Teldrassil Blasted Lands Eastern Plaguelands The Hinterlands Searing Gorge","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.6,"y":34.2,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.6,"y":91.9,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"763":{"id":763,"t":"Rites of the Earthmother","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Totem of Hawkwind to Baine Bloodhoof in Bloodhoof Village. Follow the road out of Camp Narache.\nTotem of Hawkwind\nProvided: Totem of Hawkwind","desc":"For you to continue with the Rites of the Earthmother you must pass two more tests. It is time for you to broaden your experience, ‹name›.\nTravel to Bloodhoof Village and seek out the Chief, Baine Bloodhoof, son of Cairne. There you may continue your journey and earn the acceptance of the elders of Thunder Bluff.\nTake this totem to Baine. He will recognize my carvings and help you on your path.\nFollow the road out of Camp Narache and travel with haste. Do not stray or you will lose your way.","rew":"Experience: 340\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"What brings you to my village, ‹class›?","done":"Word from my good friend, Chief Hawkwind! Ah, I can see by his carvings you are of a special breed.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":43.9,"y":76.7,"n":"Chief Hawkwind","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.7,"y":63.4,"n":"Baine Bloodhoof","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9083":{"id":9083,"t":"Bonescythe Waistguard","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -15g instead of 0.","obj":"Rohan the Assassin at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Bonescythe Waistguard if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Waistguard, 8 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 5 Cured Rugged Hides, 1 Nexus Crystal and 15 gold pieces.\nDesecrated Waistguard Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Heigan the Unclean 0 % in Naxxramas , Noth the Plaguebringer 0 % in Naxxramas\n8 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n5 Cured Rugged Hide\nNexus Crystal","desc":"If you want Bonescythe made, you're going to have to supply the materials.\nEnter Naxxramas, the big floating city of death in the sky up there, and find desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps. Bring those back along with the materials to put everything together and you'll have your Bonescythe. Oh, and you'll need to pay me for my troubles... I'll supply the bones.","rew":"You will receive:\nBonescythe Waistguard\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"How do you expect me to get anything done without the items I requested?","done":"The belt is ready, ‹name›. Have you ever seen such a high-quality item sold for so little?","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.9,"n":"Rohan the Assassin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9243":{"id":9243,"t":"Polar Tunic","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -300g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 8 Frozen Runes, 16 Enchanted Leathers, 5 Essences of Water, 5 Cured Rugged Hides and 300 gold. You must also be of Exalted reputation with the Argent Dawn.\n8 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n16 Enchanted Leather sold by Lhara\n5 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more\n5 Cured Rugged Hide\nReach 42000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"Thanks to you and Omarion, may he rest in peace, I am now able to create a Polar tunic. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nPolar Tunic","back":"Have you brought the materials?","done":"Here is your order, ‹name›. Delivered as promised!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"95803":{"id":95803,"t":"A token of good faith","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the head of Rudolph Gelhardt to Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity.\nProvided: Rudolph Gelhardt's Head","desc":"Now that we've claimed the head of the tarnished commander, I need you to deliver it to the Undercity. Sylvanas Windrunner mistrusts us greatly, and all but openly disparages us.\nDeliver Rudolph Gelhardt's head to the Dark Lady. Show her that we tend to our own house and are devoted to the prosperity of the forsaken.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Why are you addressing me, ‹class›?","done":"I don't doubt Danitha's sincerity and desire to earn a place for your kind amongst the Forsaken. However, I suspect that this isn't the last time we'll see one of your brothers and sisters go mad and turn the light against their own people.\nThere may come a time when I decide that tolerating your misbegotten order is no longer in the best interests of the Forsaken. I suggest you continue to serve your people diligently.\nWe will be watching.\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.6,"n":"Danitha Morr","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":57.8,"y":91.8,"n":"Lady Sylvanas Windrunner","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"1643":{"id":1643,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search the Trade District of Stormwind for Stephanie Turner.","desc":"Your task then, ‹name›, is to find someone here in Stormwind that is in need of aid. Someone who is pure of heart and motive. Perhaps someone helping others. Perhaps someone in need of a guide. Regardless, the person must have noble intent and be relying on your kindness.\nDo this, and return to me when you are finished. Then, we shall discuss more of your path and what it means to be a paladin of the Light.","rew":"Experience: 460","done":"Oh, hello, luv. How go your adventures? Oh, I'm so glad to hear you're doing well.\nOh, me? Thank you for asking--I'm doing well, all things considered.\nThe increase in tradesmen has kind of put a damper on the amount of leather and cloth people are willing to part with these days, so it's been tougher to make clothing for the children at the orphanage, but we'll manage. By \"we\" I mean my husband and I. He's up in Ironforge trying to seek help from the citizens there.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":63.8,"y":72.2,"n":"Stephanie Turner","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"7643":{"id":7643,"t":"Ancient Equine Spirit","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire special horse feed used for feeding a spirit horse. Merideth Carlson in Southshore apparently is the source for such food.\nTravel to the Dire Maul dungeon in Feralas and slay Tendris Warpwood. Doing so will free the Ancient Equine Spirit. Feed it the special horse feed, thereby soothing the spirit. Finally, give it the Arcanite Barding so it may bless it.\nArcanite Barding\nManna-Enriched Horse Feed\nProvided: Arcanite Barding","desc":"Your barding needs a special form of blessing, one from an appropriate spirit. In Dire Maul is such a spirit, the Ancient Equine Spirit. It is currently held by a corrupt treant, Tendris Warpwood. Pass judgment upon this foul beast, ‹name›.\nKnow this - freedom alone is not enough. You must soothe the spirit before receiving its blessing. For that, special horse feed is needed. Travel to Southshore first and speak with Merideth Carlson on this... and prepare for more sacrifice.","rew":"Experience: 4,950","back":"The Ancient Equine Spirit looks at you expectantly, as though it wants something from you.","done":"The Ancient Equine Spirit accepts the offering of the Manna-Enriched Horse Feed, nuzzling the container as it helps itself to the special oats and grains. After it has eaten a little, it looks at the barding you possess and positions itself as though it wants you to place it upon its back...\nStormwind City Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5643":{"id":5643,"t":"Shadowguard","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar.","desc":"Like many of our own priests, your own tribe puts you through rites of passage. These rites often teach priests special abilities that are vital to their survival. I sense that time is upon you even as we speak. You must return to the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar and speak to Ur'kyo. What he teaches you might be very important for the future.","rew":"You will learn: Shadowguard\nExperience: 390","done":"Your rites will come soon enough. For now, I teach you a spell that will be of great use to you when you do battle with your enemies.\nUndercity Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":49.1,"y":14.6,"n":"Father Lankester","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.6,"y":87.8,"n":"Ur'kyo","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"5723":{"id":5723,"t":"Testing an Enemy's Strength","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,150 experience instead of 850, 2.53 times as much. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Search Orgrimmar for Ragefire Chasm, then kill 8 Ragefire Troggs and 8 Ragefire Shaman before returning to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff.\nRagefire Trogg slain : 0/ 8\nRagefire Shaman slain : 0/ 8","desc":"Beneath the city of Orgrimmar, stout creatures known as troggs started coming to the surface from deep below the lava filled tunnels. In her ever-benevolence, Magatha sought to make peace with the creatures, but they turned on her diplomats, killing them. She will not allow such treatment of the tauren people and now consider the creatures a threat to all of the Horde.\nShe asks that you put an end to this trogg threat before it overwhelms the Horde from below. Find Ragefire Chasm and destroy them all.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,150\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"How goes your search for the Chasm? And the troggs?\nThe threat cannot be allowed to persist--it will only injure our orc brethren if it continues.","done":"I am glad to see you took Magatha's task seriously. Thank you, ‹name›. I'm sure the troggs will have a harder time coming to the surface with their numbers so greatly reduced.\nPerhaps in the future we can take time to figure out where such creatures came from, and what they really want.\nThunder Bluff Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":70.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Rahauro","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ragefire-chasm"]},"8843":{"id":8843,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Horde Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with Thunder Bluff. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":42.4,"y":57,"n":"Officer Thunderstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"3083":{"id":3083,"t":"Encrypted Tablet","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Encrypted Tablet and speak to Rwag in the Valley of Trials.\nEncrypted Tablet\nProvided: Encrypted Tablet","desc":"Ah, while you were gone a tablet came for you, ‹name›.\nRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the rogue trainer Rwag. He would have words with you when you're ready.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Welcome to the Valley of Trials, Rangrang. You wouldn't be here if you hadn't gotten my tablet, so I will get to the point.\nI am Rwag and I am responsible for training the rogues, thieves, and cutpurses here in the Valley. I'm the one the Hand will turn to if you're not ready for what's to come. But don't worry, the Hand won't be controlling everything you do, but it would be wise to work with them if they have need of your talents.","done":"Until such time comes, you'll be under my tutelage. I will show you the ropes as some folks say. Whenever you feel prepared, come to me and I will see about training you further. Until then, practice your skills and keep them honed to a razor's edge. You'll never know when you'll need even the most insignificant ability.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":41.3,"y":68,"n":"Rwag","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"1963":{"id":1963,"t":"The Shattered Hand","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Tazan and bring his Satchel to Therzok in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.\nTazan's Satchel Tazan","desc":"The Warchief is too subtle in his methods. He is cautious to unleash the might of the Horde. Once we were stronger, mighty conquerors all. That pride we must regain, and the Shattered Hand will do so.\nWe build strength from the shadows and strike at the exposed, secretly laying our enemies low. A task you must complete for me, to prove your worth.\nThe troll Tazan trades with the pirates near Ratchet. He has information I must have. Kill him and bring me his satchel.","rew":"Experience: 675","back":"It is a fool who believes a charge with axe drawn is more dangerous than a knife in the dark.","done":"Hm, while I am glad to hear that Tazan is no longer with us, a locked satchel does us no good. We need the information kept within.\nThis should prove a worthy second challenge for one who wishes to join the Shattered Hand.\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.7,"y":53.6,"n":"Therzok","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"7723":{"id":7723,"t":"Curse These Fat Fingers","lv":49,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Hansel Heavyhands wants you to kill 20 Heavy War Golems.\nThe Heavy War Golems wander the areas surrounding the Cauldron in the Searing Gorge. When you've killed enough, return to Hansel in Searing Gorge.\nHeavy War Golem slain : 0/ 20","desc":"Unfortunately, I can't dish out the beats like I used to, due to this here fat finger problem. Ye see, the climate out here combined with the lack o' air pressure makes me fingers expand. They're like gigantic Thelsamar Blood Sausages, they are...\nYe're gonna have to carry out me orders of business and what have ye.\nFirst on me agenda: Poundin' the livin' daylights out o' the heavy war golems o' the Gorge. Get crackin'.","rew":"You will receive:\nSlagplate Gauntlets\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,550\n+100 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"Did ye pound 'em?","done":"Ye're a good lad, ye are. I got ye a lil' present fer yer troubles.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":38.6,"y":27.8,"n":"Hansel Heavyhands","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8763":{"id":8763,"t":"The Hero of the Day","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -5g instead of 0.","obj":"Bring 1 Deeprock Salt and 5 gold coins to any Holly Preserver machine, upon which you will receive 5 Preserved Holly.\nDeeprock Salt Garr 30 % , Setis 24.5 % , Infernal Bodyguard 24.1 % , Faulty War Golem 24 % and 4 more","desc":"Listen... I'm not really supposed to be telling you this, but since you're the hero of the day and all...\nThere's fresh holly everywhere this time of the year, but it never lasts. We've got a machine that preserves holly - it never goes bad! We use it to spice up the holiday... and profits during the summer!\nI'll let you use the preserver, but only if you're a master cook. You'll need some deeprock salt and two, three, oh let's say five gold. It'll net you a nice batch that's yours to keep.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Preserved Holly","back":"The \"Holly Preserver\" machine looks like some sort of still at first, but a careful examination of it reveals some goblin-esque changes to it. Still, your skill at cooking seems to allow you to understand how the machine works.\nThere is already fresh holly in the machine - you simply need to provide some deeprock salt and five gold coins to get the machine working.","done":"The machine lets off a little rumble and a small amount of steam as it starts working. It is not too long thereafter until it stops, heralded by another small jet of steam erupting from it. A door hatch opens, revealing a batch of preserved holly!\nDun Morogh Stormwind City Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.5,"y":31.9,"n":"Wulmort Jinglepocket","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.7,"y":32,"n":"Holly Preserver","e":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.1,"y":69.5,"n":"Holly Preserver","e":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":53.6,"y":67.2,"n":"Holly Preserver","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"97243":{"id":97243,"t":"Call of fire","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Torch of Dormant Flame to Olariaan Swiftburn at the Shrine of Flames in the Gustberry Lowlands.\nProvided: Torch of the Dormant Flame","desc":"Even though we are in the realm of skywall, this is still the elemental plane. The spirits of all four elements speak to us, if we deign to listen. One among us Windshapers is in particular attunement with the element of fire. A shen'dorei by the name of Olariaan Swiftburn.\nBring this to him at the Shrine of Flames in the Gustberry Lowlands. You'll find it tucked away along the edge of the island, west of Valanaar.","back":"Yes, Nattyrav? What do you have there?","done":"So you've brought the torch. Yes, young ‹class›, I can teach you to heed the call of fire. It will not be easy, but nothing that we do in this realm is ever easy.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":58.2,"y":78.4,"n":"Sessaria Skystride","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.4,"y":44.8,"n":"Aarnor Galestrike","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":51.2,"y":86,"n":"Olariaan Swiftburn","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8283":{"id":8283,"t":"Wanted - Deathclasp, Terror of the Sands","lv":59,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Deathclasp's Pincer to Vish Kozus, Captain of the Guard.\nDeathclasp's Pincer Deathclasp","desc":"The terrible scorpid, Deathclasp, is believed to have retreated to the southern mountain range in the presence of increased silithid activity. She presents a great threat to patrols and expeditions in the southern regions. Individuals participating in her destruction will be remunerated handsomely. Inquire with Captain Vish Kozus, at the top of the Cenarion Hold Watchtower, regarding a reward.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSandstrider's Mark Black Crystal Dagger\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,050\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"I'll need the creature's pincer as proof of the deed. No pincer, no reward.","done":"Excellent! With Deathclasp gone we're free to use the southern mountain range as a strategic path to circumvent the silithid hives. Your work is greatly appreciated.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.4,"y":38.3,"n":"Wanted Poster: Deathclasp","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":50.8,"y":33.7,"n":"Vish Kozus","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8363":{"id":8363,"t":"Abyssal Signets","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Abyssal Signet The Duke of Cynders , The Duke of Fathoms , The Duke of Shards , The Duke of Zephyrs","rew":"You will receive:\nSack of Spoils\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You've shown you're more than capable of taking on an Abyssal Duke, ‹name›. I'm always one to promote good habits. Bring me more signets and I'll give you a reward.","done":"Excellent, ‹name›! Defeating those Dukes will leave the Twilight's Hammer reeling for a while. As promised, here's your reward. It's some of the better stuff Huum and I have found.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"443":{"id":443,"t":"Rot Hide Ichor","lv":17,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 bottles of rot hide ichor to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.\n8 Rot Hide Ichor Raging Rot Hide 30 % , Rot Hide Savage 30 % , Rot Hide Plague Weaver 30 % , Rot Hide Brute 30 % and 1 more","desc":"Before we launch an assault on Fenris Isle, we must determine who is behind the rot hide gnolls. Our apothecaries believe their origin lies within the strange fluid that flows through their bodies.\nGo to Fenris Isle, east of the Decrepit Ferry, and collect rot hide ichor from the gnolls you find there. Bring it to Apothecary Renferrel, stationed outside the Sepulcher.","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,250\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do you have the rot hide ichor, ‹name›?","done":"Very good. This ichor will help us understand the nature of the rot hides, and may show us their weakness...\n...if they have one.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":40.9,"n":"High Executor Hadrec","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.9,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"95883":{"id":95883,"t":"The tortured soul","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect a Tortured Soul from the nearby undead in Beren's Peril in Silverpine Forest.\nTortured Soul","desc":"<The preparations for a hastily-assembled ritual are gathered unceremoniously on the altar. According to the scrap of note, everything has been gathered. All that's missing are the offering of blood and the Tortured Soul.\nThe undead around you look tortured enough. They may have what you seek.>","back":"<The offering stone is ominously still.>","done":"<The tortured soul lets out a foul energy in the presence of the offering stone.\nIt appears you are closer to fulfilling the ritual.>","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":58.1,"y":69.9,"n":"Offering Stone","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"6523":{"id":6523,"t":"Protect Kaya","lv":18,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Kaya Flathoof to Camp Aparaje, and then return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.","desc":"Thank you for rescuing me! We must leave quickly before they discover that I am free. Please escort me to Camp Aparaje. From there, I know my way.\nMy father, Makaba Flathoof, will be desperate to know that I am safe.","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350","done":"Kaya is alive! ‹name›, I have you to thank for rescuing her.\nStonetalon Mountains The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":73.5,"y":85.6,"n":"Kaya Flathoof","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":35.2,"y":27.8,"n":"Makaba Flathoof","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"6283":{"id":6283,"t":"Bloodfury Bloodline","lv":26,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Harpy Bangles.","obj":"Maggran at Sun Rock Retreat wishes you to slay Bloodfury Ripper and bring her remains as proof of your deed.\nBloodfury Ripper's Remains Bloodfury Ripper","desc":"Limiting the number of Bloodfury Harpies will not be enough. The only true cure for their disease would be to slay their leader, Bloodfury Ripper!\nShe is all but a queen to those filthy creatures. Slay her and their numbers will surely diminish.\nGo back into the Charred Vale and you will find her along the western hills. She will not be easy to vanquish, but the reward will be great.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSpritekin Cloak Screecher Belt Harpy Bangles\nNew in Forever: Harpy Bangles.\nExperience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Bloodfury Ripper is a nasty creature! You will have success finding her along the western hill line in the Charred Vale.\nThe bloodfuries will be helpless with out... surely we can vanquish them forever!","done":"Already I feel the anger leave me. What will I do with my time? Knowing evil moves near my land kept my thoughts moving, though now they are silent. Perhaps this is a good thing... maybe now I can focus on the good, as all Tauren should.\nPlease accept this as a reward for your troubles.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":47.2,"y":61.2,"n":"Maggran Earthbinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"1083":{"id":1083,"t":"Enraged Spirits","lv":26,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Smoldering Embers from any of the fire elementals in the Charred Vale to Kaela Shadowspear in Stonetalon.\n8 Smoldering Embers Rogue Flame Spirit 10 % , Burning Destroyer 10 % , Burning Ravager 10 %","desc":"I'm unsure what the Venture Co. did to the Vale, but it's obvious they were overpowered by the creatures there.\nThey set the forest aflame, and used their inventions of destruction to decimate as much of the Vale as possible.\nBut in their ignorance they also released something else: burning spirits, elementals of flame, stone and rage.\nThe land has no chance to see Elune's smile while these creatures roam free.\nBring me their smoldering embers to show you've reduced their numbers.","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The first time I saw the Charred Vale I almost wept, ‹name›.","done":"The remains of our enemy... your strength serves us well, ‹name›. Thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.9,"y":66.8,"n":"Kaela Shadowspear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"93963":{"id":93963,"t":"Exploring the alliance","lv":13,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Randal Emerson in Stormwind Keep to receive further instructions. Use the instructions received to locate and speak with King Magni Bronzebeard, High Tinker Mekkatorque, and Tyrande Whisperwind.\nRecieve Instructions from Randal Emerson\nSpeak with High Tinker Mekkatorque\nSpeak with King Magni Bronzebeard\nSpeak with Tyrande Whisperwind","desc":"Stormwind, Ironforge, and Darnassus all have unique peoples and cultures. As a guest of the Alliance here on Azeroth, you should take some time to visit each of our capital cities in turn.\nSpeak with Randal Emerson in the southern antechamber for directions to get you started.","rew":"You will receive:\nCloak of the Honored Guest\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Stormwind\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Darnassus\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles\n+100 reputation with Kirin Tor","done":"Ah, you are back.\nI hope your adventures have given you a sense of the scale and wonder of our world. I know it must seem overwhelming to you, but if you are to help your people, you must be prepared for whatever may come your way while you are on Azeroth.\nWhile you wait for your order to establish itself in Dalaran, I suggest you turn your attention to the lands around Stormwind. Westfall in particular can always use more strong adventurers to lend them aid, if you are willing.\nStormwind City Ironforge Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78,"y":18,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"1243":{"id":1243,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":28,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give the Sealed Note to Watcher Backus in Duskwood.\nSealed Note to Watcher Backus\nProvided: Sealed Note to Watcher Backus","desc":"Jorgen, you ol' sonuva.... So, that's how it's going to be, huh?\nAll right, I can deal with that. I hope he finds the Twisting Nether that much sooner!\nHere's what's gonna happen, ‹name›. I'll start using my contacts here, but you're doing most of the footwork so I save some coin.\nHead to Darkshire in Duskwood and find Watcher Backus--he usually patrols the north road right outside of town. Just tell him you're looking into any Defias activity for me and he'll help you out with any information he can.","rew":"Experience: 230","back":"Not too safe to be traveling about in the woods, ‹name›. Be careful, and if you see anything suspicious or dangerous, contact the Watchers immediately. Don't try and take anything on yourself. We're not responsible for anything terrible that might happen to you.\nBut we both know you're gonna ignore me and fight whatever comes out of the darkness anyway, don't we? Haha, yeah, you adventurer types... all the same.","done":"Oh, Trias sent you, huh? That's a little different.\nFeel free to fight whatever monstrosities come at you from the darkness. I'm sure you'll be able to handle it pretty easily if you're the type to be hanging around with the likes of him.\nSo, what does my friend need of me on such a gloomy day as this?\nStormwind City Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":66,"y":74.1,"n":"Elling Trias","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":74.8,"y":44.2,"n":"Watcher Backus","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"203":{"id":203,"t":"The Second Rebellion","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 15 Kurzen Jungle Fighters.\nReturn to Sergeant Yohwa at the Rebel Camp.\nKurzen Jungle Fighter slain : 0/ 15","desc":"We're fighting a losing battle with Colonel Kurzen. Not only is he a brilliant tactician, he outnumbers us at least 10 to 1! To survive, we need to use his own, covert tactics against him.\nEnter his camp to the east and kill his men. Lots of them. And get out before reinforcements can close on you.","rew":"Experience: 1,950\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I hope you've been successful in your hunting, ‹name›. We won't last long against him without your help.","done":"Well done. The loss of those Jungle Fighters will relieve some of the pressure on our camp.\nBut now that you've had a taste of the forces we're up against, do you still want to throw your lot in with us??","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38,"y":3.3,"n":"Sergeant Yohwa","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"603":{"id":603,"t":"Ansirem's Key","lv":37,"min":32,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to Catelyn in Booty Bay.","desc":"The mage that is in possession of the Stone is amplifying its power through some focal point... an altar of some sort. You should be able to disrupt it by overpowering it.\nAs it happens, I know just the thing: an ancient dagger, another troll relic. There's just one... little problem.\nYou see, I found the dagger while researching in Stranglethorn, but I gave it to my willful daughter, Catelyn, who ran off to Booty Bay to become a pirate.","rew":"Experience: 1,400\n+50 reputation with Booty Bay\n-250 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","done":"My dagger? What are you, some sort of comedian?\nWhat? Do you just want me to repeat the story of how I've gone from the best knife fighter in Booty Bay to the laughing stock of piratedom!\nI lost a knife fight to one of the Bloodsail Buccaneers--bunch of right bastards they are!--and he took my blade as spoils.\nIt's not as though I can get by as a knife fighter with insults and a sharp tongue alone...\nAlterac Mountains Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":18.8,"y":78.5,"n":"Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.3,"y":77.5,"n":"Catelyn the Blade","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"5243":{"id":5243,"t":"Houses of the Holy","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Stratholme, in the north. Search the supply crates that litter the city and recover 5 Stratholme Holy Water. Return to Leonid Barthalomew the Revered when you have collected enough of the blessed fluid.\n5 Stratholme Holy Water Supply Crate in Stratholme , Stratholme Supply Crate in Stratholme","desc":"I look at my undeath as a malady, ‹race›. An illness that merely requires treatment; however, it is also a great blessing for the Argent Dawn. What better vessel to smite the heathens of the Scourge than through the undead?\nI am revered by my colleagues because of the sacrifices I have made, but the accolades mean nothing to me.\nIf you are interested in assisting the Argent Dawn, then a job I can offer.\nVenture to Stratholme and recover our surplus of holy water. Search the supply crates.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCrown of the Penitent Band of the Penitent\nYou will also receive:\n5 Superior Healing Potion 5 Greater Mana Potion\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Be wary, not all supply crates will have survived the destruction of the city. The Scourge dare not touch the water but surely the holy water will not prevent vermin infestations.","done":"Well done, ‹race›. You have proven that while you are tolerant of others, you will stop at nothing to destroy the minions of Kel'Thuzad.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.9,"y":48.3,"n":"Leonid Barthalomew the Revered","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"8923":{"id":8923,"t":"A Supernatural Device","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Sealed Venom Container to Mux Manascrambler in Gadgetzan.\nSealed Venom Container\nProvided: Sealed Venom Container","desc":"You must be quite brave to have stuck around after that. That or I've piqued your interest with the piece of armor I gave you. There is more from where that came from, if you're still interested in aiding me.\nThe venom samples you collected are for an acquaintance of mine, Mux Manascrambler, an engineer with an interest in the supernatural. His latest project consists of a device that allows you to communicate with the dead! My last hope is to contact Anthion and find out more about my situation.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"You wish to speak to me?","done":"Excellent! Just as I was running low!\nYou say Mokvar sent you?\nOrgrimmar Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Mux Manascrambler","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"923":{"id":923,"t":"Tumors","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Mossy Tumors to Rellian Greenspyre in Darnassus.\n5 Mossy Tumor Elder Timberling 42 % , Timberling Mire Beast 42 % , Timberling Trampler 35 %","desc":"There is a malevolence growing in the timberlings. We are trying to find the source, but until we do...in order to keep Teldrassil safe we must cut down the timberlings who are beyond help. Those that wander Wellspring Lake in northern Teldrassil are the most tainted. They must be removed!\nDestroy the Timberlings you find there, and gather the mossy tumors growing upon them. Bring the tumors to me so that they may be burned.","rew":"You will receive:\nPruning Knife\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 975\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you been to Wellspring Lake, ‹name›? Have you been hunting the timberlings there?","done":"Well done! These tumors are the symptom of the timberling's disease. They are filled with a poison that we must cleanse from our new land.\nI will dispose of these tumors. Thank you, ‹name›.\nDarnassus Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.2,"y":21.6,"n":"Rellian Greenspyre","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"6363":{"id":6363,"t":"Tal the Wind Rider Master","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ahanu's Leather Goods to Tal in Thunder Bluff.\nAhanu's Leather Goods\nProvided: Ahanu's Leather Goods","desc":"I have prepared leather goods for Jahan to sell at the Crossroads. Will you bring them to him?\nIf you have already been to the Crossroads and spoken to their wind rider master, then you can fly one of our Thunder Bluff wind riders back to him.\nTake the leather goods to Tal, our wind rider master in Thunder Bluff, and speak with him to arrange transport to the Crossroads.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Greetings, ‹class›. What can I do for you?","done":"You need to take this to the Crossroads, eh? That's not a problem. If you've already been there and spoken to Devrak, then you can take one of my wind riders back to him.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":45.8,"y":55.8,"n":"Ahanu","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":47,"y":49.8,"n":"Tal","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"97003":{"id":97003,"t":"Cholaruk the ravener","lv":21,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Bring the head of Chol'aruk to Gur'ak in the Barrens.\nChol'aruk's Head","desc":"You there, ‹class›. I need your aid. There are rumors of a beast that makes its lair deep in a cave at Thorn Hill, northeast of here. The Razormane call it Chol'aruk or \"The Ravener\". It's supposedly five times the size of a normal quilboar with a thirst for blood that can never be sated.\nMost don't believe the tales. But I do--because I've fought its like before.\nSeek out its lair and slay Chol'aruk. Bring me its head. I warn you though--prepare well and do not go alone.\nBlood and thunder, ‹class›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nChol'aruk's Trophy Sword Big Bad Basher Quilboar Toothpick Thornwoven Shield\nMoney: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,100\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"It took the strength of six skilled fighters to defeat one of these creatures, and it still managed to fell four of us before we could put it down.\nIf these monstrous beasts were to appear in greater numbers, the damage that the qullboar could inflict upon the land could be catastrophic.","done":"Impressive, ‹class›. None will doubt my tales when I return to Orgrimmar with this grim proof of the existence of these abominations. Rest assured this glory is yours however, and I will speak loudly of your deeds.\nLok-tar!","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.6,"y":29,"n":"Gur'ak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1483":{"id":1483,"t":"Ziz Fizziks","lv":21,"min":16,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Ziz Fizziks in Windshear Crag.","desc":"The Venture Company stole many of the best goblin minds, but from time to time, we get the opportunity to steal some back.\nA while ago, the Venture Company outfit in the Stonetalon Mountains hired Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle--a gnome! Their other engineer, Ziz Fizziks, was so taken aback by this, he pleaded with me to find him new employment with the Tinkers' Union. I set him on a few tasks, but he might need help.\nMaybe you could look in on him for me? He's stationed at the western edge of Windshear Crag.","rew":"Experience: 420\n+25 reputation with Ratchet","done":"I thought those Venture Company higher-ups were slave drivers, but then I met Sputtervalve, the cruelest of them all!\nHa! Though it's better than being out of a job, I suppose... Or worse, working with that Gerenzo. If you're here to help, I've got something for you to do.\nThe Barrens Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":63,"y":37.2,"n":"Sputtervalve","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59,"y":62.6,"n":"Ziz Fizziks","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"843":{"id":843,"t":"Gann's Reclamation","lv":23,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gann Stonespire wants you to kill 15 Bael'dun Excavators and 5 Bael'dun Foremen.\nBring Khazgorm's Journal to Gann Stonespire.\nKhazgorm's Journal Prospector Khazgorm\nBael'dun Excavator slain : 0/ 15\nBael'dun Foreman slain : 0/ 5","desc":"In solitude I wander these roads.\nThe dwarves of Bael Modan show no respect for my land. Horrendous blasts drive holes deep into the ground as noisy machines rip apart the hills. Lands which once served as home and provider to my tribe are now riddled with destructive dwarves.\nAttempts at reaching a diplomatic resolution have failed. Now is the time for decisive action.\nDrive the dwarves from the Bael Modan excavation by force and bring to me the journal of their leader, Prospector Khazgorm.","rew":"Money: 15 0 gold, 15 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,850\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Many innocent tauren lost their lives or were forced off their ancestral birthplace when the dwarves of Bael Modan arrived. My land must be reclaimed!","done":"Khazgorm met the fate he earned. I feel no remorse for the fool. He was an infidel on these lands.\nMay his death serve as a warning to all those who threaten to disrupt our way of life.\nNow let me take a moment to study the dwarf's journal....","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":45.9,"y":77,"n":"Gann Stonespire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"363":{"id":363,"t":"Rude Awakening","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Shadow Priest Sarvis.","desc":"About time you woke up. We were ready to toss you into the fire with the others, but it looks like you made it.\nI am Mordo, the caretaker of the crypt of Deathknell. And you are the Lich King's slave no more.\nSpeak with Shadow Priest Sarvis in the chapel at the base of the hill, he will tell you more of what you must know.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Undercity","done":"Another of the walking dead, hm? Must have been quite a shock, waking up in the crypt with only the cold and Mordo to greet you...\nI see the confusion on your face. Let me try to explain our... situation... to you.\nWe have been freed from the control of the Lich King by our new leader, Lady Sylvanas. The Dark Lady guides us in our war against the hated Scourge and the holdouts of humanity who dog our every step.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.2,"y":71.7,"n":"Undertaker Mordo","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.8,"y":66.2,"n":"Shadow Priest Sarvis","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"2283":{"id":2283,"t":"Necklace Recovery","lv":41,"min":37,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Look for a valuable necklace within the Uldaman dig site and bring it back to Dran Droffers in Orgrimmar. The necklace may be damaged.\nShattered Necklace Stonevault Cave Hunter 8 % , Stonevault Oracle 8 % , Stonevault Rockchewer 8 % , Shadowforge Digger 8 % and 2 more","desc":"We've got work for you, that is if you've got the guts to do it!\nDeep in the Badlands is the Uldaman dig site. We've heard a tale about some idiot paladin who died there recently. Why we even care is that he had a very valuable necklace on him. It's supposedly got three large gems: a ruby, a sapphire, and a topaz.\nThe shot: we want it, and we're payin' TOP SILVER to get it. It may be damaged, but that's neither here nor there; we'll fix whatever scratches are on it.","rew":"Experience: 2,450\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Well, do you have the necklace? You won't see a copper from us if you don't have that necklace!","done":"Mmmm salvage! I can smell the necklace from here. Now let's look at that beauty...\nHey, what do you think you're trying to do here? This necklace is missing the gems! You think we wouldn't notice? Even Malton could see that the gems are gone.\nWell, maybe you didn't steal them... but this necklace is worthless without those gems! Your job isn't done here yet, not by a long shot!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":59.6,"y":36.5,"n":"Dran Droffers","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"3883":{"id":3883,"t":"Alien Ecology","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,100 experience instead of 3,050, 1.67 times as much.","obj":"Use the Scraping Vial to collect a Hive Wall Sample from one of the Gorishi hive hatcheries in Un'Goro Crater. Look for the chambers with the hanging larval spawns.\nBring the Hive Wall Sample to Hol'anyee Marshal in Un'Goro Crater.\nHive Wall Sample\nProvided: Unused Scraping Vial","desc":"Just because we've suffered a setback doesn't mean that research must stop! We were investigating the Gorishi insects in the southern part of the crater before winding up here. Their presence is alien to the ecology of Un'Goro, and we want to find out why.\nIn their hive network must be larval hatcheries. You can identify these places by their hanging larval spawns. Use this vial to take a sample of the hive wall near any of the hatcheries. Bring it back to me for study, but be careful!","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100","back":"Do you have the sample of the Gorishi hive for me to study, ‹name›?","done":"Yes, this will do nicely. You've been a great help... I wish I could give you more than this, but being virtually stranded in the middle of a savage land does limit what I can and cannot give. Rest assured though - the research done here would not have been possible without your assistance!","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":43.9,"y":7.2,"n":"Hol'anyee Marshal","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"1803":{"id":1803,"t":"Tome of the Cabal","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 600 experience instead of 2,450, 0.24 times as much.","obj":"Retrieve the Moldy Tome and Tattered Manuscript for Jorah Annison in the Undercity.\nMoldy Tome Tome of the Cabal\nTattered Manuscript Damaged Chest","desc":"Ah! I see that you are a warlock of similar tastes to mine. Indeed, acquiring the Tome of the Cabal is a worthy aspiration. Did you know that it was once held within the walls of Lordaeron? It was vandalized though, almost half its pages removed. Who would commit such a heinous act?\nThat half is lost, though rumor says that it fell into the hands of the centaur of the Thousand Needles.\nThe rest of the text was to be transferred to Ironforge, but was lost in transit on the coast west of Southshore.","rew":"Experience: 600","back":"It may be that you are chasing after fairy tales, ‹name›, but truth can be found at the center of even the wildest rumors.","done":"Well well well! What do we have here?\nThis is impressive, ‹name›. I wouldn't have thought it possible, but here it is in my very hands, the complete Tome of the Cabal.\nAllow me to leaf through its pages for just a moment before you are off again.\nUndercity Hillsbrad Foothills The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":75.9,"y":37.9,"n":"Jorah Annison","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"7563":{"id":7563,"t":"Rage of Blood","lv":58,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 30 bottles of Raging Beast's Blood to Mor'zul Bloodbringer in the Burning Steppes.\n30 Raging Beast's Blood Berserk Owlbeast 35 % , Moontouched Owlbeast 35 % , Crazed Owlbeast 35 % , Ragged Owlbeast 35 % and 1 more","desc":"The dreadsteeds dwell on another world, on the fiery Plains of Xoroth, and to bind one of those famed beasts you must invoke powerful glyphs. I can scribe the glyphs on a parchment for you, but first I will need a special ink.\nIn distant Winterspring there dwells a race of owl beasts. Once pure creatures, they were turned mad by the demonic emanations of the Darkwhisper Gorge and now roam the snows in a frenzy.\nTheir blood is what I need to ink your parchment. Bring it to me.","rew":"Experience: 7,750","back":"Have you seen the raging owl beasts, ‹name›? The magic of those creatures is strong, and it concentrates in the blood that flows through their torturted forms.","done":"Ah, very good. I will have this blood distilled into an ink and use it for the parchment I promised you. And perhaps I will save just a little for myself, as I hear its taste is quite euphoric...\nBurning Steppes Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.7,"y":31.6,"n":"Mor'zul Bloodbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"5403":{"id":5403,"t":"Invader's Scourgestones","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Invader's Scourgestone Lorekeeper Polkelt in Scholomance , Rattlegore in Scholomance , Blood Steward of Kirtonos in Scholomance , Terrordale Spirit 35 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nArgent Dawn Valor Token\nExperience: 550\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"An Invader's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's elite troops. These are sometimes found on the stronger of the troops positioned in the Plaguelands. Slaying such a creature is indeed a challenge, but one that should be relished with a commission to vanquish evil.\nThe Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for ten of these insignia. Bring them to me here, and I will make sure you receive your just reward.","done":"Congratulations, ‹name› - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!\nEach valor token handed out to worthy recipients is a sign of the tide turning against the Scourge. With more and more heroes fighting the Scourge in their own lands, the Argent Dawn will assuredly be at the forefront when the time comes to wage war on the ultimate evil of the Scourge. I hope that the valor you've shown what it took to acquiring your token will carry the day then as well!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":83.5,"n":"Argent Officer Pureheart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5803":{"id":5803,"t":"Araj's Scarab","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy Araj the Summoner and bring Araj's Scarab to Alchemist Arbington at Chillwind Point, Western Plaguelands.\nAraj's Scarab Araj's Phylactery","desc":"Araj the Summoner lords over Andorhal from the ruined city's heart. We know that he was the former leader of Scholomance before claiming the city as his own. To finish the key, we will need his signet - called a scarab - mounted as the head of the key.\nMake your way into the heart of Andorhal, and break his hold on the city now that he is drawn into the open. Once destroyed, seize his scarab from his fallen phylactery!\nThe Key to Scholomance awaits, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 4,950","back":"You've come this far ‹name› - only the destruction of the physical form of Araj the Summoner will provide us with the means to finish the key. Get Araj's scarab, by hook or by crook, and bring it to me - I will fuse it on as the head of the key.","done":"Yes, this is it! I... again, I'm absolutely amazed at the depths of your cunning and bravery. It simply boggles the mind the lengths you are willing to go in order achieve victory.\nAllow me now to play my small part in this. I've prepared a special solvent that should allow me to secure the scarab on as the head of the key, infusing it with the power to breech the locked door of Scholomance.\nThis should take just a moment...","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":83.8,"n":"Alchemist Arbington","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"98283":{"id":98283,"t":"Carnage","lv":30,"min":22,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Carnage's Head to Rethiel the Greenwarden in The Green Belt.\nMalignant Rotclaw Flesh\nCarnage's Head","desc":"The natural order of this land is breaking. Once it was that the Razormaw raptors kept the land from overgrowth. They now live in fear of their alpha, named only for the carnage it leaves behind.\nI fear the beast has been driven mad by the sickness that we have yet to fully excise.\nIt will respond to the malignant flesh of the diseased bears below Raptor Ridge, to the northeast. Leave their entrails in its cave lair.\nCarnage will come. Bring me its head.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRazormaw Shorts Carnage Trousers\nExperience: 3,050","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":56.2,"y":40.4,"n":"Rethiel the Greenwarden","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"6603":{"id":6603,"t":"Trouble in Winterspring!","lv":56,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Donova Snowden near the hot springs in Winterspring.","desc":"There's trouble in Winterspring!\nWhy, sure, I spend some time out in the wilds and know about these things... I'm always mighty proud to say it. I consider the hours I spend out there in the hills to be golden. Help you cultivate quick reflexes, a cool head and a keen eye...\nIt takes judgement, brains and maturity to appreciate the wilderness in the way that I do.\nNow, what was I talking about?\nAh yes, trouble. See Donova Snowden at the hot springs and she can tell you more.","rew":"Experience: 575","done":"Well, hi there! So Meggi told you of the trouble I have found here?","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":60.7,"y":38.2,"n":"Meggi Peppinrocker","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5083":{"id":5083,"t":"Winterfall Firewater","lv":56,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Empty Firewater Flask to Donova Snowden in Winterspring.\nEmpty Firewater Flask Winterfall Runner 10 % , Winterfall Pathfinder 10 % , Winterfall Totemic 10 % , Winterfall Den Watcher 10 % and 2 more\nProvided: Empty Firewater Flask","desc":"This vial that you picked up from the Winterfall furbolg is empty, but you can detect a few drops of a strange green liquid inside; it almost glows.\nIs it something important?\nDonova Snowden would probably be able to tell you more, since she has been camped by the hot springs in Winterspring for some time now.","rew":"Experience: 2,900\n+50 reputation with Everlook","back":"What is that you have found?","done":"You got this from the Winterfall?","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5163":{"id":5163,"t":"Are We There, Yeti?","lv":58,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Umi's Mechanical Yeti and scare her friends with it:\nLegacki in Everlook (Winterspring)\nSprinkle in Gadgetzan (Tanaris)\nQuixxil in Marshal's Refuge (Un'Goro Crater)\nWhen you are done, bring the Mechanical Yeti back to Umi.\nUmi's Mechanical Yeti\nScare Legacki\nScare Sprinkle\nScare Quixxil\nProvided: Umi's Mechanical Yeti","desc":"It's all ready, ‹name›!\nNow, I sent some mail to my friends already, telling them that I have a surprise for them. This is where you come in!\nI'm going to give you my mechanical yeti, and you need to surprise them by paying each of my friends a visit, turning the yeti on and sending it towards them.\nOnce you have shown Legacki in Everlook, Sprinkle in Gadgetzan, and Quixxil in Marshal's Refuge, come back and tell me what happened!\nPlease bring my yeti back to me then, too.","rew":"You will receive:\nMechanical Yeti\nMoney: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,750\n+150 reputation with Everlook","back":"I can't wait to hear how my friends react!\nThey'll never expect it!","done":"Hah! They'll think twice before making fun of my ideas again!\nThanks for your help, ‹name›. I couldn't have had so much fun without you!\nWinterspring Tanaris Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":60.9,"y":37.6,"n":"Umi Rumplesnicker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92683":{"id":92683,"t":"Flutterfly dust","lv":9,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gather 5 Flutterfly Dust from the Flutterflies around the Gustberry Lowlands.\n5 Flutterfly Dust\nProvided: Flutterfly Swatter","desc":"I'm sure you've noticed the giant flutterflies out in the outer fields near the orchard? They are pleasant to look at, but they also have other benefits; namely their wing dust. It can be a mess, but if you can gather it up in large amounts, it has useful household applications.\nTake this Flutterfly Swatter and give the big bugs a good swat for me. They'll usually just get scared and flee, but sometimes they'll take some offense. Either way, they'll give their rumps a shake and drop a pile of dust.","rew":"You will receive:\nFlutterfly Swatter 5 Minor Mana Potion\nExperience: 600","back":"Flutterflies are normally docile and calm, but rub them the wrong way and sometimes they'll surprise you.","done":"This stuff can be a bit messy and it tends to get everywhere. You'll probably be shaking this out of your trousers for weeks, unfortunately. I do appreciate it, though. I've had this on my to-do list for weeks, but getting too far from the house when it's just me on my own with bandits lurking everywhere is a big risk.\nDon't bother asking me what I use this stuff for. Things. Stuff and things. Don't worry about it.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":46.6,"y":81.8,"n":"Aamelia Windfield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8043":{"id":8043,"t":"Strength of Mount Mugamba","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Strength of Mugamba","rew":"You will receive:\nStrength of Mugamba\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Master ‹name›, you return! Molthor has sent word of your deeds to the King. Your name is known even in the South Seas. Perhaps one day you will be a legendary ‹class› - a story for the ages.\nGive me your talisman so that I may once more amplify its power.","done":"Use your newfound strength to destroy the Gurubashi!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});